From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:10:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): a deburr leaves each edge run straight up before
 travelling

Each run opened with a rapid from the previous run's end - cone still in
the break it cut - diagonally to the next start at the clearance plane,
through the part (#304). The path now retracts vertically first, the
same move it already made after the last run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
